{
 "comment": "Bot chat visibility table. Rows are history rows (role, text, sender.kind, steered, ownerMessage, needsYou, messageId); expected is the verdict per row after the rule in server/bot-view.ts. The panel DOM rule (rc-chat.js botRowVisibility/botRowKind) must give the same verdicts: role user = .msg.user, assistant = .msg.assistant, action = .act, error = .banner.err, notice = .notice, ownerMessage = an owner bubble (keep). A steered user row never starts a turn.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "name": "an owner turn shows everything",
   "rows": [
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "u:owner"
    },
    {
     "role": "action",
     "text": "Bash ls"
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "r"
    }
   ],
   "expected": [
    "show",
    "show",
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "a recap or autopilot turn is the owner's: shown",
   "rows": [
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "u:recap",
     "sender": {
      "kind": "recap"
     }
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "r"
    },
    {
     "role": "user",
     "text": "u:autopilot",
     "sender": {
      "kind": "autopilot"
     }
    },
    {
     "role": "assistant",
     "text": "r"
    }
   ],
   "expected": [
    "show",
    "show",
    "show",
    "show"
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "a digest hides everything",
